<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <!-- The published API reference is generated from the `///` comments in
             this project, so they have to survive compilation. -->
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <!-- The doc comments are written in Markdown — backticks, lists,
             emphasis — so the reference has to read them that way rather than
             printing the punctuation. -->
        <UsesMarkdownComments>true</UsesMarkdownComments>
        <!-- 11001 is the `CompilerMessage` on the handful of members that only
             exist because an inline operator's body has to reach them. The
             message is for a consumer reaching for one by mistake; in here
             the operators themselves are the callers. -->
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);11001</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Warp11.Designs.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!-- What makes this package this package. Everything shared with the two
         debugger packages — version, licence, repository, symbol settings — is
         in `hdl/Directory.Build.props`, because a version written once cannot
         disagree with itself. -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <PackageId>Warp11</PackageId>
        <Description>An F# hardware description language that runs on real FPGAs. One source elaborates a cycle-accurate simulator, a step-through debugger, synthesizable Verilog, and the register-map seam a host driver compiles against — so what you debug is what you deploy. Includes typed ready/valid streams, a numeric layer carrying width, fraction bits and signedness, AXI4-Lite and AXI4 masters, and low-FIRRTL import and export.</Description>
        <PackageTags>fpga;hdl;verilog;fsharp;simulation;hardware;rtl;firrtl;xilinx</PackageTags>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>Breaking, and safe to take: every function that returned an anonymous record now returns a named type — WrapCounter, MemReadPort, EdgeDetect, AxiLiteChannel, the audio port records and the rest. Field names are unchanged, so source that reads .count or .data still compiles; anything compiled against alpha.1 must be recompiled. The payoff is that those fields now carry documentation, which ships in the package as XML and reaches your editor. Also: doc comments on the whole public surface, and several that were silently attached to the wrong declaration are now on the right one. Narrowed for 0.1.0: Warp11.Ir no longer exports signal, signalS, litAt, declOf, refs, asUnsignedType or asSignedType; Warp11.Dsl no longer exports StateMachineRecord, and Builder keeps only the seven members a moduleDef body uses (Input, Output, Wire, Reg, RegNoReset, If, Instance) — the ambient functions (memWrite, assertThat, withDomain and the rest) are the surface, and they work inside moduleDef too. isNamed, agreeOnSign, declareWire, declareReg and declareRegNoReset stay public only because inline operators reach them: they are hidden from completion and from the reference, and a direct use reports message 11001 naming what to use instead.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- The repo README is the package's front page too. Packed to the
             root, which is where nuget.org looks for it. -->
        <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <Compile Include="Ir.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Keywords.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Crossings.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Board.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Mapping.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Format.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Layout.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Dsl.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Combinators.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Streams.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="AxiLite.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="RegMap.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Number.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="NumberOperators.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Verilog.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Flatten.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Firrtl.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="FirrtlImport.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Inventory.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Sim.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="SimDevice.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="SimAxi.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="SimStream.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Breakpoint.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Debug.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Catalog.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Vcd.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Diff.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Stdlib.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Uart.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="SerialRegMap.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="SimUart.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Windows.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Bands.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Audio.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Pdm.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="SimI2s.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Wav.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="SimPdm.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Pgm.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Csv.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Fu.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Units.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Pedal.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="BoardTop.fs"/>
        <Compile Include="Build.fs"/>
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
